  "raw": {
    "https://wit.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Boston-MA-US/Visiting-Assistant-Professor--Civil-Engineering--Surveying-Geomatics_JR5450": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Professor, Civil Engineering, Surveying/Geomatics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Visiting Assistant Professor, Civil Engineering, Surveying/Geomatics Wentworth Institute of Technology is seeking applicants who are interested in joining the Wentworth community for on a per semester basis: Surveying/Geomatics in Fall 2026 This will be a full-time Visiting Assistant Professor in the Douglas D. Schumann School of Engineering in Fall 2026, with an opportunity to apply for a full-time Assistant Professor position for Fall 2027. Please email Associate Dean   Anuja   Kamat   kamata@wit.edu   if you have any questions. The standard load for the position is 16 credit hours per semester for the Fall 2026 semester. Extension into the spring semester, based on coursework availability and needs will be considered, alongside evaluation of performance and potential interest.   Required Qualifications: Master's degree in Civil Engineering or equivalent Preferred Qualifications: Ph.D. degree in Civil Engineering or equivalent Position Details:    It is expected that the salary range for this position is between $34,000 and $38,000 for one semester. The specific pay for this position will be determined by the University based on consideration of all relevant factors when and if it decides to extend an offer of employment.  The position does not include a comprehensive benefits package. Please be aware that any final offer for this position is contingent on the applicant providing valid I-9 documentation, showing work authorization and identity.  Compensation and Benefits Wentworth Institute of Technology is committed to fair, transparent, and legally compliant compensation practices. We believe that clarity about pay structures and ranges supports equity, fosters trust, and ensures a positive workplace for all employees. Please visit here to see the comprehensive benefits package offered to support the best experience for our employees. https://wit.edu/careers/work-wentworth Inclusive Excellence at Wentworth Inclusive Excellence is one of the four pillars of the Strategic Plan. Actively and intentionally cultivating a diverse and culturally competent institution where each member has the opportunity and support to reach their full potential and make contributions to our campus community and beyond is Inclusive Excellence at Wentworth. To find out more about the Wentworth’s commitment to Inclusive Excellence, please visit the website https://wit.edu/about/inclusive-excellence . All applicants have the right to accessibility support and accommodations. To request accessibility support or accommodations, contact the Executive Director of Equity and Compliance, Catlin Wells, at wellsc1@wit.edu . E-Verify for Employment Eligibility Verification ( Form I-9) Wentworth participates in E-Verify. E-Verify is an internet-based system that compares information from your Form I-9 to records available to the U.S. Department of Homeland Security (DHS) and Social Security Administration (SSA) to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States."
    },
    "https://wit.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Boston-MA-US/Administrative-Assistant--School-of-Architecture-and-Design_JR5312-1": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant, School of Architecture and Design",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-20\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Administrative Assistant - School of Architecture & Design, Wentworth Institute of Technology The School of Architecture & Design (SoAD) at Wentworth Institute of Technology invites applications for a full-time Administrative Assistant position beginning  Fall 2026 . The Administrative Assistant serves as a primary point of contact for the School, providing outstanding customer service and administrative support to students, faculty, staff, alumni, and external partners. This position plays a vital role in the daily operations of the School and contributes to a collaborative, student-centered environment. Reporting to the School Operations Manager, the Administrative Assistant works closely with the Dean's Office, Associate Dean, Program Directors, faculty, and staff to support academic programs, school operations, events, communications, and strategic initiatives. Application   Requirements:    Applicants must submit the following in a  single PDF  document in the Resume Attachment Section:   1) Cover letter (1 page) describing areas of expertise and qualifications   2) Current curriculum vitae    3) Contact information for three professional references. Candidates will be notified before the University contacts their references   About Wentworth and the School of Architecture and Design   Wentworth Institute of Technology is a co-op university located in the heart of Boston, Massachusetts, with a strong emphasis on experiential learning and academic excellence. The university includes five schools: Architecture and Design, Computing and Data Science, Engineering, Management, and Sciences and Humanities. Wentworth is a member of the Colleges of the Fenway consortium, providing opportunities for collaboration and resource sharing with nearby institutions, including Massachusetts College of Art & Design and Simmons University.  Wentworth is a university with a teaching focus and strategic initiatives of diversity, equity, and inclusive excellence, high-value learning, transformational student experience, and next-generation partnerships. The school has a strong commitment to recruiting and retaining students with diverse backgrounds, fostering a vibrant design community and learning environment for faculty and students, and building on and expanding current government, community, industry, and alumni partnerships. For more information about Wentworth’s Strategic Plan, see:  https://wit.edu/about/strategic-plan   Wentworth’s School of Architecture and Design (SoAD) recognizes the critical role its courses and curriculum play in fostering academic success and addressing equity gaps. We seek new faculty to join a community committed to teaching excellence, curricular innovation, and mentoring of students. SoAD offers highly respected Bachelor of Sciences degrees in Industrial Design (NASAD accredited), Interior Design (CIDA accredited), Architecture, Master of Architecture (NAAB accredited), and Building Sciences. The mission of the SoAD is to empower design students and educators from all backgrounds to become creative, civic-minded problem-solvers, responding to global challenges and contributing to local communities. The SoAD guides students to engage locally and globally, explore advanced technologies, collaborate within and across disciplines, gain industry experience via cooperative education, and learn to design sustainably and equitably. The school comprises approximately 940 undergraduate and 100 graduate students, 34 full-time and approximately 70 adjunct faculty, and 5 full-time staff. The Dean’s office includes an associate dean, three program directors, a program coordinator, an operations manager, and a director of labs. Responsibilities: Serve as the first point of contact for students, faculty, staff, and visitors, responding to inquiries and directing requests appropriately. Provide administrative support to the Dean, Associate Dean, Program Directors, faculty, and graduate students. Assist with graduate program administration, communications, and events Support the management of studio, classroom, and office spaces, including scheduling and coordination. Coordinate School events, including final reviews, exhibitions, lectures, town halls, commencement-related activities, and other community gatherings. Coordinate the collection, cataloging, archiving, and documentation of student work and maintain records of School events and activities for future planning and historical archives. Manage and update content for the School's website, digital communications, and social media platforms. Assist with the logistics of undergraduate semester study-abroad programs, M.Arch Global Research Studios, faculty-led travel, and other domestic and international student travel experiences. Support admissions and recruitment initiatives, including Open Houses, Welcome Days, Pre-College programs, SummerFAB, and K–12 outreach activities. Provide administrative support for School publications and externally facing communications, including  Making Masters , the M.Arch thesis collection, and the  Wentworth Design Review . Assist faculty with community engagement initiatives, industry partnerships, and special projects. Support data collection, reporting, and accreditation-related activities as needed. Perform other duties and special projects as assigned to support the mission and strategic priorities of the School. ** Review of applications will begin on August 31, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. For more information, please contact Keeran Hariprasad: hariprasadk@wit.edu Minimum Education: Bachelor's degree Minimum Work Experience: One to three years of experience in a customer service, administrative, higher education, or comparable professional environment. Minimum Qualifications: Excellent organizational, interpersonal, communication, and customer service skills. Strong attention to detail and the ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Experience coordinating events, managing projects, and collaborating effectively with diverse teams. Proficiency with Microsoft Office, Google Workspace, and other web-based communication and collaboration platforms. Ability to work independently while contributing to a collaborative, service-oriented team. Strong written communication skills and the ability to maintain accurate records and documentation. Preferred Education: Bachelor's degree in design, communications, or a related field. Master's degree. Preferred Qualifications: Experience working in higher education. Demonstrated interest in design or other creative disciplines. Experience with website content management systems and social media platforms. Demonstrated graphic design skills (Adobe Creative Suite, Canva, or similar software). Familiarity with generative AI tools and their application to communications, administrative workflows, and content creation. Experience supporting events, exhibitions, or public programs. Position Details:    At this time, the university is unable to sponsor applicants for H-1B visas. The job grade for this position is Grade 3N. The expected hourly range for this position is between $25.64 - $29.74 which reflects what we reasonably expect to pay for this role. This position is a 37.5-hour work week schedule. This is an in-person position that requires the incumbent to be on site daily. This position is not eligible for remote work. This position comes with a 10% retirement contribution . Compensation and Benefits Wentworth Institute of Technology is committed to fair, transparent, and legally compliant compensation practices. We believe that clarity about pay structures and ranges supports equity, fosters trust, and ensures a positive workplace for all employees. Please visit here to see the comprehensive benefits package offered to support the best experience for our employees. https://wit.edu/careers/work-wentworth Inclusive Excellence at Wentworth Inclusive Excellence is one of the four pillars of the Strategic Plan. Actively and intentionally cultivating a diverse and culturally competent institution where each member has the opportunity and support to reach their full potential and make contributions to our campus community and beyond is Inclusive Excellence at Wentworth. To find out more about the Wentworth’s commitment to Inclusive Excellence, please visit the website https://wit.edu/about/inclusive-excellence . All applicants have the right to accessibility support and accommodations. To request accessibility support or accommodations, contact the Executive Director of Equity and Compliance, Catlin Wells, at wellsc1@wit.edu . E-Verify for Employment Eligibility Verification ( Form I-9) Wentworth participates in E-Verify. E-Verify is an internet-based system that compares information from your Form I-9 to records available to the U.S. Department of Homeland Security (DHS) and Social Security Administration (SSA) to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States."
    },
    "https://wit.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Boston-MA-US/Network-Engineer-I_JR5294": {
      "title": "Network Engineer I",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-19\nPosted: Posted 16 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Network Engineer is responsible for the design, development, optimization, security, performance, reliability, and ongoing support of Wentworth Institute of Technology’s wired and wireless network infrastructure. This role manages the full lifecycle of network devices and systems, including routers, switches, firewalls, cabling, wireless access points, and controllers. Key responsibilities include planning, designing, and implementing network infrastructure projects, working both independently and collaboratively with cross-functional teams. This involves engaging stakeholders to gather requirements, coordinating internal and external resources, developing and presenting network designs, overseeing project implementation, and maintaining comprehensive network documentation. Reporting to the Director of IT Infrastructure and Security, the Network Engineer works closely with the Information Security Officer and IT Security team to ensure compliance with security best practices. This includes utilizing tools such as Network Access Control (NAC) to develop, implement, and enforce security policies and controls across the wired and wireless network environment. Essential Functions Design, implement, and optimize wired and wireless network infrastructure for the Wentworth campus, including all residential, academic, and service buildings, including both new network installations and the refresh of existing network installations with new technology. Serve as a technical point of contact for any university projects that include a networking component. Ensure that the design implemented optimizes the network experience of students, faculty, and staff while providing a highly redundant, secure, and reliable network infrastructure. Respond to, troubleshoot, and resolve any network related issues or problem. Proactively identify potential network problems using the network monitoring and analysis tools available and develop and implement plans to remediate issues. Review incident tickets and respond to client requests and issues in a timely fashion and with a high level of customer service. Develop documentation and training for both the Tech Spot and for end users to provide faster resolution of common issues and to optimize the use of the network. Implement, optimize, and maintain network monitoring and alerting applications and tools. Monitor the usage, capacity, and reliability of various network related systems and plan steps needed to resolve issues and sustain the network infrastructure for current and future applications. Identify utilization patterns and their effects on Internet traffic and plan effective ways to maintain the highest quality of service possible. Maintain network monitoring and management system and ensure reporting is accurate. Create, update, and maintain design documentation of all network systems, including but not limited to structured cabling, wiring closets, network switches and routers, wireless APs and controllers. Create knowledge base documentation for common network related issues or procedures, as well as training documentation for first level Tech Spot support staff and for other network support staff. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Engineering, or related field, or a combination of education, relevant work experience, and professional certifications—such as industry-recognized credentials or international degree equivalencies—may be accepted in place of a bachelor’s degree. Minimum 3-5 years of relative experience implementing and supporting critical network infrastructure and technology. In depth understanding of Local Area Network (LAN) and Wide Area Network (WAN) technologies and protocols. In depth understanding of wireless networking protocols and standards (802.11). Experience implementing, optimizing, and maintaining network monitoring and alerting applications and tools. Experience working on a technical team, collaborating with other teams and departments, and providing guidance and leadership to other technical team members. Demonstrated record of providing a high level of customer service for end users and responding to any interruption of service with an appropriate sense of urgency. Demonstrated knowledge of Internet of Things (IOT) devices and terminology. Experience supporting and implementing them on an enterprise network. Preferred Qualifications Minimum of 5+ years of relative experience implementing and supporting critical network infrastructure and technology. Experience deploying and supporting HP/Aruba routers and switches. Experience deploying and supporting HP/Aruba wireless access points, mobility controllers, and network access control (Clearpass). Experience in developing implementation plans and network designs for refreshing network hardware and incorporating new technologies. Experience designing, analyzing, optimizing, and troubleshooting Wi-Fi networks. Ability to present technical information clearly and understandably to a diverse set of individuals and groups on campus. Experience with Palo Alto Networks firewalls. Familiarity with higher education-specific networking needs (dense residential deployments, IoT support, research networks). Knowledge of multi-ISP environments and hybrid cloud connectivity. Certifications such as Aruba Certified Switching Professional (ACSP), Aruba ClearPass Certified, Palo Alto PCNSA/PCNSE, CCNA, or equivalent. Work Environment While this position is often office-based and sedentary, the Network Engineer must regularly move throughout buildings, offices, data center space, and telecommunication closet to install, inspect, troubleshoot and maintain network equipment.  The role may often require lifting or carrying equipment or tools weighing up to 20 pounds. Position Details The job grade for this position is Grade 8.  The expected salary for this position is between $78,000 - $98,000 which reflects what we reasonably expect to pay for this role. At this time, the university is unable to sponsor applicants for H-1B visas for this position. This position is a 37.5-hour work week schedule. This is an in-person position that requires the incumbent to be on site daily. This position is not eligible for remote work. Compensation and Benefits Wentworth Institute of Technology is committed to fair, transparent, and legally compliant compensation practices. We believe that clarity about pay structures and ranges supports equity, fosters trust, and ensures a positive workplace for all employees. Please visit here to see the comprehensive benefits package offered to support the best experience for our employees. https://wit.edu/careers/work-wentworth Inclusive Excellence at Wentworth Inclusive Excellence is one of the four pillars of the Strategic Plan. Actively and intentionally cultivating a diverse and culturally competent institution where each member has the opportunity and support to reach their full potential and make contributions to our campus community and beyond is Inclusive Excellence at Wentworth. To find out more about the Wentworth’s commitment to Inclusive Excellence, please visit the website https://wit.edu/about/inclusive-excellence . All applicants have the right to accessibility support and accommodations. To request accessibility support or accommodations, contact the Executive Director of Equity and Compliance, Catlin Wells, at wellsc1@wit.edu . E-Verify for Employment Eligibility Verification ( Form I-9) Wentworth participates in E-Verify. E-Verify is an internet-based system that compares information from your Form I-9 to records available to the U.S. Department of Homeland Security (DHS) and Social Security Administration (SSA) to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States."
    },
    "https://wit.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Boston-MA-US/Program-Director--School-of-Computing-and-Data-Science_JR5158": {
      "title": "Director - CS, Cybersecurity, and IT Programs",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 18 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Wentworth Institute of Technology’s School of Computing and Data Science is seeking a forward-thinking Director to lead our undergraduate and graduate programs in [B.S. in Computer Science, B.S. in Cybersecurity, B.S. in Information Technology, M.S. in Applied Computer Science, and M.S. in Cybersecurity] in collaboration with faculty and school leadership. Reporting to the Dean, the Program Director plays a key role in curriculum development, accreditation, program assessment, and student success. Key Responsibilities: Oversee curriculum planning, assessment, and accreditation. Support Dean and Associate Dean in scheduling, faculty assignments, and academic standards. Support student advising, recruitment, and retention efforts. Collaborate with university offices such as Registrar, Marketing, and COOPS+CAREERS. Teach up to 3 courses during the academic year and 2 in summer for additional pay. Assist with strategic planning, budgeting, and program communications. Contribute to strategic planning, budgeting, and program communications as a member of the Dean's leadership team. The ideal candidate will have strong leadership skills, experience in academic administration, and a passion for student-centered education. Minimum Requirements : Doctoral degree or equivalent terminal degree in Computer Science, Cybersecurity, Information Technology, or Education with a strong quantitative or computing focus, or a closely related field. Exceptional candidates with an ABD (All but Dissertation) status or a relevant Master’s degree plus significant teaching or research experience will also be considered. 3+ years of experience in teaching, research, or programmatic contributions in academic, industry, or public sector settings. Comprehensive knowledge and understanding of higher education and its challenges and opportunities Experience in serving students, management, and leadership Record of clear research and scholarship agenda Record of commitment to inclusive excellence. Preferred Requirements: Preferred Education: Doctoral degree in Computer Science, Cybersecurity or Information Technology. Preferred Work Experience Required: 5–8 years of progressive responsibility in academic, research, or equivalent roles, including teaching, program development, or leadership. Experience in a tenure-track or teaching-intensive role is a plus but not required. Prior experience as a full-time faculty member in a tenure-track, tenured, or comparable academic appointment, with demonstrated understanding of faculty responsibilities, academic governance, and curriculum development, is strongly preferred. Record of excellence in pedagogy and curriculum development Record of excellence in leadership and management Record of excellence in working in a collaborative environment We value diverse career paths and encourage applicants from industry, government, or interdisciplinary academic backgrounds who demonstrate commitment to teaching, innovation, and student success. Candidates who bring experience in inclusive pedagogy, emerging technologies, or cross-disciplinary collaboration are especially encouraged to apply. Be a part of a team shaping the future of higher education. Apply by sending a cover letter and CV to this posting. Position Details: The job grade for this position is Grade 11. The expected salary for this position is between $120,000 - $150,000 which reflects what we reasonably expect to pay for this role. At this time, the university is unable to sponsor applicants for H-1B visas. The preferred start date for this position is as soon as practicable. We recognize that candidates may need to provide appropriate notice to their current institution or employer and are prepared to accommodate a reasonable transition period. About Wentworth & the School of Computing and Data Science:   Wentworth is an institution known as a university of opportunity with a high return on investment for its graduates. Our mission is to empower, inspire, and innovate through experiential learning and a student-centered approach to education.   The School of Computing & Data Science consists of 30+ full-time faculty that offer undergraduate majors in Computer Science, Cybersecurity, IT, Data Science, and Applied Mathematics and graduate degrees in Computer Science, Data Science, and Cybersecurity. The school has teaching and research strengths in artificial intelligence, data science, cybersecurity, high-performance computing, mobile/web application development, stochastic processes, dynamical systems, financial math and modeling. In addition, members of the school have close collaborative relationships with faculty in sciences, humanities, and electrical and computer engineering, among others.   Our faculty comprises individuals from wide-ranging backgrounds and experiences, where collaboration is highly encouraged and supported, and our School has no department boundaries. Another point of pride is that our faculty members include those with significant industrial, consulting, entrepreneurial, and project management experience.  Compensation and Benefits Wentworth Institute of Technology is committed to fair, transparent, and legally compliant compensation practices. We believe that clarity about pay structures and ranges supports equity, fosters trust, and ensures a positive workplace for all employees. Please visit here to see the comprehensive benefits package offered to support the best experience for our employees. https://wit.edu/careers/work-wentworth Inclusive Excellence at Wentworth Inclusive Excellence is one of the four pillars of the Strategic Plan. Actively and intentionally cultivating a diverse and culturally competent institution where each member has the opportunity and support to reach their full potential and make contributions to our campus community and beyond is Inclusive Excellence at Wentworth. To find out more about the Wentworth’s commitment to Inclusive Excellence, please visit the website https://wit.edu/about/inclusive-excellence . All applicants have the right to accessibility support and accommodations. To request accessibility support or accommodations, contact the Executive Director of Equity and Compliance, Catlin Wells, at wellsc1@wit.edu . E-Verify for Employment Eligibility Verification ( Form I-9) Wentworth participates in E-Verify. E-Verify is an internet-based system that compares information from your Form I-9 to records available to the U.S. Department of Homeland Security (DHS) and Social Security Administration (SSA) to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States."
    },
    "https://wit.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Boston-MA-US/Head-Coach--Women-s-Lacrosse_JR5284": {
      "title": "Head Coach, Women's Lacrosse",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 18 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Position Summary Wentworth Institute of Technology invites applications for the position of Head Women’s Lacrosse Coach. This full-time, 12-month administrative position provides leadership for all aspects of the University's NCAA Division III women’s lacrosse program, including student-athlete development, competitive success, recruitment, program administration, and strategic planning. Consistent with Wentworth's strategic priorities of Inclusive Excellence, Transformative Student Experience, and High-Value Learning, the Head Coach creates an environment where students are challenged academically, athletically, and personally while representing Wentworth with professionalism, integrity, and a commitment to the University's mission and values. The Head Coach serves as an educator, mentor, and leader who develops a culture of accountability, belonging, teamwork, competitive excellence, and continuous improvement. The successful candidate will provide strategic leadership for all aspects of the program while developing student-athletes, hiring, supervising, mentoring, and evaluating assistant coaches, collaborating with colleagues across the University, responsibly stewarding program resources, and strengthening relationships with alumni, supporters, and external partners in support of the long-term success of Wentworth Women’s Lacrosse. Required Application Materials: Resume and Cover Letter. Professional references are recommended. Scope of Responsibility Program Leadership & Administration Provide strategic leadership and administrative oversight for all aspects of the NCAA Division III women’s lacrosse program, establishing competitive goals, setting program expectations, and cultivating a positive, accountable, and student-centered team culture. Oversee the day-to-day operations of the program, including: Planning and conducting practices Preparing for competition Developing game strategy Scheduling contests Coordinating team travel Overseeing equipment management Evaluating program performance Manage the program budget, support fundraising and alumni engagement initiatives, and fulfill all fiscal and administrative responsibilities in a timely and responsible manner. Recruit, supervise, and mentor a part-time assistant coaching staff by providing ongoing mentorship, regular feedback, and opportunities for professional development. Recruitment & Enrollment Recruitment at Wentworth is viewed as the foundational step of long-term student retention and success. The Head Women’s Lacrosse Coach provides strategic leadership for recruiting and roster management that reflects the values of Wentworth Institute of Technology and the Wentworth Athletics Department. Working collaboratively with Enrollment Management and Athletics and Student Affairs leadership, develop and execute an annual recruiting strategy that supports institutional and program enrollment goals while identifying student-athletes who will thrive academically, socially, and competitively at Wentworth. Cultivate relationships with prospects and their families, clearly articulating the unique value of a Wentworth education and the University's commitment to student success and professional development. Student-Athlete Development Beyond competition, the Head Coach is committed to the holistic development of student-athletes by promoting academic success, leadership development, personal well-being, and competitive excellence. Partner actively with cross-institutional colleagues to support student well-being, academic achievement, leadership development, personal accountability, and overall student success. Encourage student-athletes to engage fully in the academic, leadership, and co-curricular opportunities available through the University. Departmental & Institutional Engagement Alongside primary coaching duties, full-time head coaches are assigned a secondary duty or administrative responsibility that is reviewed and assigned annually based on the candidate’s qualifications, seasonal responsibilities, and department needs. Support Athletics Department operations through game management responsibilities, conference and NCAA championship administration, and departmental signature events. Serve as an active member of the Division of Student Affairs and the Athletics Department by contributing to divisional and departmental planning, committee work, collaborative initiatives, and a shared commitment to student-athlete success. Build and maintain collaborative relationships with faculty, staff, and departments across the University to support student success and advance departmental, divisional, and institutional priorities. Represent Wentworth Athletics and the University at institutional, conference, alumni, community, and professional events, serving as a positive ambassador for the athletics department and the University. Compliance & Professional Responsibilities Maintain required certifications, complete mandatory institutional training, and fulfill administrative responsibilities in a timely manner. Ensure compliance with NCAA Division III legislation, Conference of New England policies, University policies, and all applicable federal and state regulations. Qualifications Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree required. Minimum of four years of demonstrated success coaching lacrosse, including progressive leadership responsibilities. Demonstrated ability to recruit and retain academically qualified student-athletes. Valid driver's license. Demonstrated strong communication skills and experience building inclusive team environments. Preferred Qualifications Master's degree. Collegiate coaching experience at the NCAA level. Five years of collegiate coaching experience with previous head coaching or significant assistant coaching leadership responsibilities. Position Details The job grade for this position is Grade 7. The expected salary for this position is between $71,000.00 - $85,000.00 which reflects what we reasonably expect to pay for this role. At this time, the university is unable to sponsor applicants for H-1B visas.   Compensation and Benefits Wentworth Institute of Technology is committed to fair, transparent, and legally compliant compensation practices. We believe that clarity about pay structures and ranges supports equity, fosters trust, and ensures a positive workplace for all employees. Please visit here to see the comprehensive benefits package offered to support the best experience for our employees. https://wit.edu/careers/work-wentworth Inclusive Excellence at Wentworth Inclusive Excellence is one of the four pillars of the Strategic Plan. Actively and intentionally cultivating a diverse and culturally competent institution where each member has the opportunity and support to reach their full potential and make contributions to our campus community and beyond is Inclusive Excellence at Wentworth. To find out more about the Wentworth’s commitment to Inclusive Excellence, please visit the website https://wit.edu/about/inclusive-excellence . All applicants have the right to accessibility support and accommodations. To request accessibility support or accommodations, contact the Executive Director of Equity and Compliance, Catlin Wells, at wellsc1@wit.edu . E-Verify for Employment Eligibility Verification ( Form I-9) Wentworth participates in E-Verify. E-Verify is an internet-based system that compares information from your Form I-9 to records available to the U.S. Department of Homeland Security (DHS) and Social Security Administration (SSA) to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States."
    },
    "https://wit.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Student-Success-Advisor_JR4460": {
      "title": "Student Success Advisor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 21 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Position Summary: Wentworth Institute of Technology’s Integrated Advising Collaborative (IAC) Student Success Advisors (SSAs) are key members of a coordinated, student-centered advising team. SSAs partner closely with Co-op & Career Advisors (CCAs) and Faculty Advisors (FAs) to provide proactive, holistic support that connects academic planning, personal development, and career readiness throughout the student lifecycle. Student Success Advisors serve as the primary point of contact for academic planning and progression, helping students develop clear, achievable pathways to graduation. Through a developmental advising philosophy, SSAs empower students to make informed decisions, build self-advocacy skills, and connect their academic experience to long-term goals. As part of the IAC model, Student Success Advisors contribute to a shared advising structure that ensures coordinated communication, timely interventions, and a seamless student experience from matriculation through graduation. Responsibilities: Academic Advising & Coaching: Provide individualized and group advising on academic planning, degree requirements, policies, and registration. Support students in developing and maintaining academic plans aligned with timely graduation. Coach students in study skills, time management, decision-making, and self-advocacy. Assist students in navigating transitions, including first-year adjustment, major exploration, and academic challenges. Student Success & Case Management: Monitor academic progress and identify students in need of additional support. Provide outreach in response to alerts, progress reports, and advising triggers. Support students on academic probation through structured intervention plans and ongoing coaching. Connect students with campus resources including tutoring, accessibility services, and wellness support. Student Engagement Across the Lifecycle: First Year: Support transition, academic onboarding, and early engagement. Second Year: Guide academic planning and readiness for co-op preparation. Third Year: Support academic progression during co-op participation and course sequencing. Fourth Year: Ensure degree completion and support post-graduation planning. Integrated Advising Collaboration: Collaborate with CCAs and Faculty Advisors to deliver coordinated, holistic student support. Participate in joint advising meetings, case reviews, and shared success planning. Maintain shared advising notes and contribute to aligned communication strategies. Ensure seamless referrals and coordinated handoffs across the advising team. School & Faculty Partnership: Serve as an integral member of the School Advising Team within assigned school(s). Collaborate with faculty and academic leadership on student success strategies. Align advising with curriculum requirements and program pathways. Documentation & Compliance: Maintain accurate, timely advising records in institutional systems (e.g., Navigate, Banner). Ensure documentation meets institutional standards for quality and timeliness. Monitor academic standing and progression benchmarks. Professional Development & Continuous Improvement: Participate in required IAC training and professional development. Engage in assessment and continuous improvement initiatives. Stay current on advising practices, student development theory, and institutional systems. Qualifications: Required: Master’s degree in Higher Education, Counseling, or related field. 2–4 years of experience in academic advising, student support, or related field. Strong communication, organizational, and collaboration skills. Commitment to working with diverse student populations. Preferred: Experience with academic advising technologies (e.g., EAB Navigate, Banner) Familiarity with developmental advising and NACADA competencies Position Details: At this time, the university is unable to sponsor applicants for H-1B visas.     This is an in-person position with core hours of 8:30 AM–4:30 PM or 9:00 AM–5:00 PM. Specific hours and remote work must be approved by your supervisor. Occasional weekend hours may be required for Success Studio, advising, or university events.        The job grade for this position is Grade 5.             The expected wage range for this position is between $58,000 and $70,000 which reflects what we reasonably expect to pay for this role.   Compensation and Benefits Wentworth Institute of Technology is committed to fair, transparent, and legally compliant compensation practices. We believe that clarity about pay structures and ranges supports equity, fosters trust, and ensures a positive workplace for all employees. Please visit here to see the comprehensive benefits package offered to support the best experience for our employees. https://wit.edu/careers/work-wentworth Inclusive Excellence at Wentworth Inclusive Excellence is one of the four pillars of the Strategic Plan. Actively and intentionally cultivating a diverse and culturally competent institution where each member has the opportunity and support to reach their full potential and make contributions to our campus community and beyond is Inclusive Excellence at Wentworth. To find out more about the Wentworth’s commitment to Inclusive Excellence, please visit the website https://wit.edu/about/inclusive-excellence . All applicants have the right to accessibility support and accommodations. To request accessibility support or accommodations, contact the Executive Director of Equity and Compliance, Catlin Wells, at wellsc1@wit.edu . E-Verify for Employment Eligibility Verification ( Form I-9) Wentworth participates in E-Verify. E-Verify is an internet-based system that compares information from your Form I-9 to records available to the U.S. Department of Homeland Security (DHS) and Social Security Administration (SSA) to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States."
    },
    "https://wit.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Boston-MA-US/Adjunct-Instructor--Construction-Management_JR5274": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Construction Management",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 21 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob Description Adjunct Faculty Pool – Sweeney Programs of Construction Management: Wentworth Institute of Technology invites applications for part-time Adjunct Faculty positions in the School of Management’s Sweeney Programs of Construction Management for Fall 2026 and/or Spring 2027. Required Application Materials: Resume and Cover Letter of Course Interest At this time, we are particularly looking for candidates interested in teaching: Surveying Labs Building Construction Labs Construction Estimating Construction Project Management Plan Reading Building Systems Quality Control & Assurance Wentworth values student-centered, hands-on, project-based, technical education. Questions may be directed to Mr. Michael D’Agostino, Construction Management Programs Administrator. Email: dagostinom1@wit.edu . Minimum Qualifications:   Master's degree Preferred Qualifications: Doctoral degree 3 years teaching experience Significant industry-related work experience will also be considered About Wentworth and the Sweeney Programs of Construction Management: Wentworth Institute of Technology is located in Boston, Massachusetts, and comprises the Schools of Architecture and Design, Computing and Data Science, Engineering, Management, and Sciences and Humanities. Wentworth is a member of the Colleges of the Fenway consortium - an association of Boston institutions, including Emmanuel College, Simmons University, Massachusetts College of Art, and Massachusetts College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences. One of the many opportunities afforded to faculty is the ability to collaborate across these institutions and share resources.    Wentworth is a university with a teaching focus and strategic initiatives of diversity, equity and inclusive excellence, high-value learning, transformational student experience, and next-generation partnerships. The school has a strong commitment to recruiting and retaining students with diverse backgrounds, fostering a vibrant design community and learning environment for faculty and students, and building on and expanding current government, community, industry, and alumni partnerships. For more information about Wentworth's Strategic Plan, see: https://wit.edu/about/strategic-plan   The Sweeney Programs of Construction Management offers an ACCE-accredited Bachelors degree program in Construction Management with concentrations in Infrastructure and Real Estate and Facilities Management. In addition to the undergraduate program in construction management, the Sweeney Programs of Construction Management also offers two graduate programs in Construction Management and Facilities Management. Position Details:  At this time, the university is unable to sponsor applicants for H-1B visas. Adjunct faculty compensation varies based on instructional mode (lecture or lab), number of course credits, and program. The minimum adjunct rate is $1,684 per credit.   Compensation and Benefits Wentworth Institute of Technology is committed to fair, transparent, and legally compliant compensation practices. We believe that clarity about pay structures and ranges supports equity, fosters trust, and ensures a positive workplace for all employees. Please visit here to see the comprehensive benefits package offered to support the best experience for our employees. https://wit.edu/careers/work-wentworth Inclusive Excellence at Wentworth Inclusive Excellence is one of the four pillars of the Strategic Plan. Actively and intentionally cultivating a diverse and culturally competent institution where each member has the opportunity and support to reach their full potential and make contributions to our campus community and beyond is Inclusive Excellence at Wentworth. To find out more about the Wentworth’s commitment to Inclusive Excellence, please visit the website https://wit.edu/about/inclusive-excellence . All applicants have the right to accessibility support and accommodations. To request accessibility support or accommodations, contact the Executive Director of Equity and Compliance, Catlin Wells, at wellsc1@wit.edu . E-Verify for Employment Eligibility Verification ( Form I-9) Wentworth participates in E-Verify. E-Verify is an internet-based system that compares information from your Form I-9 to records available to the U.S. Department of Homeland Security (DHS) and Social Security Administration (SSA) to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States."
    },
    "https://wit.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Adjunct-Instructor--Architecture_JR5262": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Architecture",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-11\nPosted: Posted 24 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob Description Adjunct Faculty Appointments The School of Architecture and Design (SoAD) seeks multiple part-time adjunct instructors for Fall 2026 to teach undergraduate and graduate architecture courses. Current openings include ARCH2100: History/Theory 01, ARCH 9200: Research Methods, and ARCH 7910: Principles of Passive House Design. ARCH 2100 (undergraduate) and ARCH 9200 (graduate) are coordinated, multi-section courses, while ARCH 7910 is a graduate elective. The fall semester begins on September 8th and ends on December 8th, followed by the final exam period. Course information is provided below: ARCH 2100: History/Theory 01 (on-campus, in-person) Meets on Tuesday and Thursday, 1:00-2:45pm or 3:00-4:45pm 4 credits ARCH 9200: Research Methods (on-campus, in-person) Meets on Wednesday and Friday, 10:00-11:45am 4 credits ARCH 7910: Principles of Passive House Design (synchronously online) Meets on Tuesday and Thursday, 8:00-9:45am 4 credits About Wentworth and the School of Architecture and Design (SoAD) Wentworth Institute of Technology is a co-op university located in the heart of Boston, Massachusetts, with a strong emphasis on experiential learning and academic excellence. The university includes five schools: Architecture and Design, Computing and Data Science, Engineering, Management, and Sciences and Humanities. Wentworth is a member of the Colleges of the Fenway consortium, providing opportunities for collaboration and resource sharing with nearby institutions, including Massachusetts College of Art & Design and Simmons University.  Wentworth is a university with a teaching focus and strategic initiatives of diversity, equity, and inclusive excellence, high-value learning, transformational student experience, and next-generation partnerships. The school has a strong commitment to recruiting and retaining students with diverse backgrounds, fostering a vibrant design community and learning environment for faculty and students, and building on and expanding current government, community, industry, and alumni partnerships. For more information about Wentworth’s Strategic Plan, see:  https://wit.edu/about/strategic-plan Wentworth’s School of Architecture and Design (SoAD) recognizes the critical role its courses and curricula play in fostering academic success and addressing equity gaps. We seek new faculty to join a community committed to teaching excellence, curricular innovation, and mentoring of se SoAD offers highly respected Bachelor of Science degrees in Industrial Design (NASAD-accredited), Interior Design (CIDA-accredited), Architecture, and Building Sciences, and a Master of Architecture (NAAB-accredited). The SoAD’s mission is to empower design students and educators from all backgrounds to become creative, civic-minded problem-solvers, responding to global challenges and contributing to local communities. Students engage locally and globally, explore advanced technologies, collaborate within and across disciplines, gain industry experience via cooperative education, and learn to design sustainably and equitably. Comprising approximately 940 undergraduate and 100 graduate students, the SoAD has robust international study opportunities at both the graduate and undergraduate levels. About the Architecture Program:   Wentworth’s Bachelor of Science in Architecture (B.S. Arch) program offers a rigorous studio-centered curriculum emphasizing design, technology, and community engagement. Students explore architecture across scales, functions, and contexts, with concentrations in Urbanism, Emerging Technologies, and Adaptive Interventions. The Architecture programs and faculty are deeply rooted in the Boston community and have a long history of partnering with community, government, and institutional organizations. Two required cooperative education experiences bridge academic and professional practice.  The Master of Architecture (M.Arch) is a one-year, NAAB-accredited, STEM-designated program that prepares students to be leaders in a rapidly evolving profession. Through Global Research Studios and a structured thesis sequence, students engage pressing challenges in the built environment through an international lens.  To learn more about the Architecture programs, please visit the  BSArch  and  MArch  program pages.  Minimum Qualifications: Master of Architecture degree Preferred Qualifications: Flexibility in teaching approach to address diverse student needs and interests Prior university-level teaching experience Doctorate degree How to Apply: Applicants should submit the following in a single PDF document: Cover letter that outlines qualifications for the position Current curriculum vitae Position Details:   At this time, the university is unable to sponsor applicants for H-1B visas. Adjunct faculty compensation varies based on instructional mode (lecture or lab), number of course credits, and program. The minimum adjunct rate is $1,365 per credit. Compensation and Benefits Wentworth Institute of Technology is committed to fair, transparent, and legally compliant compensation practices. We believe that clarity about pay structures and ranges supports equity, fosters trust, and ensures a positive workplace for all employees. Please visit here to see the comprehensive benefits package offered to support the best experience for our employees. https://wit.edu/careers/work-wentworth Inclusive Excellence at Wentworth Inclusive Excellence is one of the four pillars of the Strategic Plan. Actively and intentionally cultivating a diverse and culturally competent institution where each member has the opportunity and support to reach their full potential and make contributions to our campus community and beyond is Inclusive Excellence at Wentworth. To find out more about the Wentworth’s commitment to Inclusive Excellence, please visit the website https://wit.edu/about/inclusive-excellence . All applicants have the right to accessibility support and accommodations. To request accessibility support or accommodations, contact the Executive Director of Equity and Compliance, Catlin Wells, at wellsc1@wit.edu . E-Verify for Employment Eligibility Verification ( Form I-9) Wentworth participates in E-Verify. E-Verify is an internet-based system that compares information from your Form I-9 to records available to the U.S. Department of Homeland Security (DHS) and Social Security Administration (SSA) to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States."
    },
    "https://wit.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Boston-MA-US/Library-Administrative-Coordinator_JR5253-1": {
      "title": "Library Administrative Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-03\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Library Administrative Coordinator The Douglas D. Schumann Library & Learning Commons seeks a highly organized, customer and detail-oriented individual to fill the role of Library Administrative Coordinator. Reporting to the Library Director, and working closely with library colleagues throughout the department, this role provides clerical and administrative support for the Schumann Library on a variety of fronts. This is a full-time, benefited position that supports scheduling, budgeting, interdepartmental communication, and event planning and coordination. This is a majority on-site position; the typical weekly schedule will be four days fully on-campus, and one-day fully remote. Required Application Materials: Resume and Cover Letter Administrative & Clerical Support (35%) Serve as the primary administrative support resource for library operations. Coordinate meeting room scheduling, support recruitment activities, and facilitate employee onboarding and orientation processes. Deliver administrative support to library staff as needed to ensure efficient departmental operations. Coordinate reimbursement processing and maintain related documentation for staff, employment candidates, and visitors. Provide comprehensive administrative support including calendar management, meeting coordination, note-taking, special project support, Microsoft SharePoint organization, and records maintenance. Act as a principal liaison for contractors and service providers. Fiscal Management & Budget Support (25%) Monitor library budgets and expenditures to ensure financial accuracy, fiscal responsibility, and compliance with institutional policies. Reconcile monthly expenditures and credit card statements in a timely and accurate manner. Manage purchasing activities, including order placement, receipt of goods, and invoice processing in accordance with established procedures. Schedule and Calendar Support (15%) Lead the coordination, maintenance, and ongoing management of library staff schedules in collaboration with library administrators. Ensuring the library website and departmental calendars reflects the most up-to-date library operating hours and events. Facilities, Equipment & Operations (15%) Coordinate facility maintenance requests, custodial services, and repair activities to support the effective operation of library spaces. Serve as the primary liaison between the Library and maintenance and custodial personnel. Serve as the primary liaison between the Library and the Copy Center to facilitate service requests and operational needs. Monitor library equipment to ensure proper functionality and arrange maintenance or repairs as necessary. Maintain inventory levels and oversee the ordering of library-owned office supplies. Collaborate with DTS to oversee computer maintenance and repair services. Stakeholder & Community Support (10%) Serve as the primary point of contact for student and campus partner requests related to library programming and room reservations. Assist with the planning, budgeting, and logistical coordination of special events, including staff recognition activities and library programming space scheduling. Required Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Candidates must be able to demonstrate the knowledge, skills, and abilities necessary to perform the essential functions of the position safely and effectively, with or without reasonable accommodation. Specifically: Proven and demonstrable commitment to providing excellent customer service. Excellent verbal and written communication skills, with the ability to build and maintain professional, collaborative, and diplomatic relationships with campus constituents and external partners. Demonstrated commitment to advancing the college’s values of inclusive excellence, diversity, equity, access, and belonging. Familiarity with basic accounting practices, budget administration, and fiscal management processes. Proficiency with standard office productivity software and the ability to learn and effectively utilize specialized library and institutional systems. Strong administrative and office support skills, including proofreading, business writing, and the application of appropriate grammar, spelling, and correspondence standards. Exceptional organizational skills, meticulous attention to detail, and the ability to manage multiple priorities while meeting deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Demonstrated ability to prioritize responsibilities, respond effectively to interruptions, and maintain productivity in a dynamic, collaborative work setting. Ability to exercise sound judgment, initiative, and problem-solving skills with an appropriate level of independence. Capacity to respond effectively to unexpected situations and changing circumstances while exercising independent judgment within established policies and procedures. High degree of professionalism, discretion, and integrity, with a demonstrated ability to handle confidential and sensitive information appropriately. Flexibility and adaptability in managing evolving priorities, operational needs, and organizational objectives. Minimum Qualifications Minimum of Associate’s Degree required. Minimum of 1-3 years of experience providing administrative support in a professional office environment. An equivalent combination of relevant education, training, and professional experience may be considered. The Schumann Library values the many pathways through which individuals develop their knowledge, skills, and expertise. We welcome applicants from diverse professional and educational backgrounds and encourage candidates to highlight how their experiences have prepared them to contribute successfully in this role. Preferred Qualifications Experience working in a library, academic library, or related educational environment. Familiarity with emerging technologies in administrative and scheduling support. Willingness to participate in campus partnerships and outreach initiatives on occasional evenings and weekends. Position Details At this time, the university is unable to sponsor applicants for H-1B visas. The job grade for this position is Grade 3N. The expected hourly range for this position is between $25.64 - $29.74 which reflects what we reasonably expect to pay for this role. Compensation and Benefits Wentworth Institute of Technology is committed to fair, transparent, and legally compliant compensation practices. We believe that clarity about pay structures and ranges supports equity, fosters trust, and ensures a positive workplace for all employees. Please visit here to see the comprehensive benefits package offered to support the best experience for our employees. https://wit.edu/careers/work-wentworth Inclusive Excellence at Wentworth Inclusive Excellence is one of the four pillars of the Strategic Plan. Actively and intentionally cultivating a diverse and culturally competent institution where each member has the opportunity and support to reach their full potential and make contributions to our campus community and beyond is Inclusive Excellence at Wentworth. To find out more about the Wentworth’s commitment to Inclusive Excellence, please visit the website https://wit.edu/about/inclusive-excellence . All applicants have the right to accessibility support and accommodations. To request accessibility support or accommodations, contact the Executive Director of Equity and Compliance, Catlin Wells, at wellsc1@wit.edu . E-Verify for Employment Eligibility Verification ( Form I-9) Wentworth participates in E-Verify. E-Verify is an internet-based system that compares information from your Form I-9 to records available to the U.S. Department of Homeland Security (DHS) and Social Security Administration (SSA) to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States."
    },
    "https://wit.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Boston-MA-US/Co-op---Career-Advisor_JR5247": {
      "title": "Co-op & Career Advisor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-03\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Position Summary: Wentworth Institute of Technology’s Co-ops & Careers department is looking for a Co-op & Career Advisor (CCA) to join our Integrated Advising Collaborative (IAC). In this role, you’ll work as part of a coordinated advising team, alongside Academic and Faculty Advisors, to help students build career readiness skills, connect their academic experience to professional pathways, and successfully complete Wentworth’s cooperative education requirement. Cooperative Education is the cornerstone of a Wentworth undergraduate degree. All undergraduate students must complete two co-op semesters as a graduation requirement, and your work will directly support their success in that process. Required Application Materials: Resume and Cover Letter Responsibilities: 1. Career Advising Provide individualized and group advising on topics such as, but not limited to career exploration and goal setting, resume, cover letter, portfolio development, interview preparation, job search strategies, networking, etc. Help students articulate skills, experiences, and goals Deliver career readiness content workshops and programming 2. Co-op Support Prepare students for participation in co-op, including teaching a co-op preparation course Guide students through identifying, applying for, and securing co-op opportunities Track student progress toward co-op eligibility and maintain accurate records Provide coaching throughout the co-op search and decision-making process 3. Integrated Advising Collaborate closely with Academic and Faculty Advisors to provide coordinated, holistic student support Participate in joint advising meetings, case reviews, and shared student success planning Contribute to consistent advising through shared documentation and aligned outreach 4. Student Engagement Across the Lifecycle First Year: Introduce career exploration and early engagement opportunities Second Year: Deliver co-op preparation programming Third Year: Support students during co-op, review evaluations, and facilitate reflection Fourth Year: Provide advanced job search and career transition support 5. Student Support & Case Management Identify students who need additional support and provide timely outreach Participate in at-risk student case reviews within the IAC Provide timely outreach in response to alerts, progress reports, and advising triggers Connect students with appropriate campus resources 6. Documentation & Compliance Maintain accurate, timely advising records in institutional systems Uphold advising standards for response time, documentation and engagement 7. School & Faculty Partnership Serve as an embedded advisor within assigned academic school(s) Build relationships with faculty and academic leadership Align advising with curriculum and program-specific pathways 8. Professional Development & Continuous Improvement Participate in required IAC training and professional development activities Stay current on workforce trends, recruiting practices, and career technologies Contribute to assessment and continuous improvement initiatives Qualifications: Required: Bachelor’s degree 2-4 years of relevant experience in career advising, co-op programs or student support Strong coaching, communication, and collaboration skills Preferred: Master’s degree in Higher Education, Counseling, or related field Experience in experiential learning or cooperative education models Familiarity with advising or CRM platforms (e.g., Navigate, Symplicity) Position Details: This is a full-time, benefits-eligible position with a 37.5-hour work week. The role is based in Boston and follows a hybrid work model, with the specific schedule determined by business needs. At this time, the university is unable to sponsor applicants for H-1B visas. The job grade for this position is Grade 7. The expected salary for this position is between $71,000.00 - $85,000.00 which reflects what we reasonably expect to pay for this role. Compensation and Benefits Wentworth Institute of Technology is committed to fair, transparent, and legally compliant compensation practices. We believe that clarity about pay structures and ranges supports equity, fosters trust, and ensures a positive workplace for all employees. Please visit here to see the comprehensive benefits package offered to support the best experience for our employees. https://wit.edu/careers/work-wentworth Inclusive Excellence at Wentworth Inclusive Excellence is one of the four pillars of the Strategic Plan. Actively and intentionally cultivating a diverse and culturally competent institution where each member has the opportunity and support to reach their full potential and make contributions to our campus community and beyond is Inclusive Excellence at Wentworth. To find out more about the Wentworth’s commitment to Inclusive Excellence, please visit the website https://wit.edu/about/inclusive-excellence . All applicants have the right to accessibility support and accommodations. To request accessibility support or accommodations, contact the Executive Director of Equity and Compliance, Catlin Wells, at wellsc1@wit.edu . E-Verify for Employment Eligibility Verification ( Form I-9) Wentworth participates in E-Verify. E-Verify is an internet-based system that compares information from your Form I-9 to records available to the U.S. Department of Homeland Security (DHS) and Social Security Administration (SSA) to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States."
    },
    "https://wit.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Boston-MA-US/Career-and-Workforce-Pathways-Specialist--Electrical-and-Clean-Energy-_JR5233": {
      "title": "Career and Workforce Pathways Specialist (Electrical and Clean Energy)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-31\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob Description Position Overview: Wentworth Institute of Technology seeks a student-centered Career and Workforce Pathways Specialist to support learners enrolled in the Massachusetts Board-approved Journeyman Electrical (JE) Program and the forthcoming Climate Critical Electrical Pre-Apprenticeship Program (CCEPA). This role will provide individualized career advising, workforce readiness support, employer engagement, and placement coordination to help students successfully transition into apprenticeship programs, employment, and continued education pathways aligned with apprenticeship to journeyman-level electrician roles and Massachusetts climate and clean energy related workforce needs. The Career and Workforce Pathways Specialist will play a key role in advancing equitable access to high-quality careers in the electrical and high-performance building sectors by supporting individuals who may face barriers to workforce entry, including early-career learners, career changers, and students from low-income or underserved communities. The position aligns directly with Wentworth’s workforce development mission and MassCEC Equity Workforce Grant objectives.  Key Responsibilities: Student Advising & Career Coaching Provide individual career coaching and goal-setting support for students enrolled in JE, CCEPA programs, and other workforce development initiatives, as needed. Provide critical feedback on application materials, resume development, interviewing skills, networking strategies, and job search preparation.  Design and deliver group workshops and training sessions on career readiness topics including but not limited to resume writing, interviewing, professional communication, networking, job search strategies, workplace expectations, and navigating apprenticeship and employment pathways. Support students in understanding apprenticeship pathways, licensing requirements, and career opportunities within the electrical and clean energy sectors.  Maintain regular student check-ins to support persistence, retention, and successful program completion.  Employer & Industry Engagement Develop and maintain relationships with employers, apprenticeship programs, unions, workforce boards, and industry partners.  Coordinate with faculty to schedule employer site visits, guest speakers, informational interviews, and networking opportunities.  Assist with apprenticeship and job placement coordination.  Identify emerging workforce trends and hiring opportunities within construction trades and climate-critical industries including electrification, EV infrastructure, renewable energy, and high-performance buildings.  Collaborate with Wentworth staff who provide external relations, such as UA, C&C, Government Relations. Administrative & Reporting Responsibilities Maintain accurate student records using Navigate360  Assist with grant reporting, participant engagement and outcomes tracking, and employer engagement documentation, as needed.  Participate in related meetings, administrative systems training, and other workforce development initiatives as needed.  Qualifications: Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree, recognized skilled-trades credential, or an equivalent combination of education, training, and relevant professional experience. Minimum of 5 years of relevant professional experience in career services, workforce development, apprenticeship, adult education, employer engagement, talent development, or a related field. Familiarity with pathways to employment for skilled trades, construction, electrical, or clean energy industries.  Demonstrated experience developing and/or delivering career-readiness workshops, training, or group programming. Experience providing career coaching, advising, or employment-related support to adult learners, job seekers, apprentices, or other workforce populations. Preferred Qualifications Knowledge of Massachusetts apprenticeship, workforce development, or occupational licensing systems. Experience building relationships with employers, unions, apprenticeship sponsors, workforce boards, or community-based organizations. Experience using student tracking or CRM systems.  Desired Attributes: Ability to motivate and support diverse learners. Strong problem-solving and case management skills. Commitment to applied, hands-on education and student success. About the Programs: Wentworth’s Journeyman Electrical Program is a Massachusetts Board-approved electrical education pathway designed to prepare students for licensure and long-term careers in the electrical industry. The Climate Critical Electrical Pre-Apprenticeship Program is a new two-stage workforce initiative focused on preparing learners for careers in electrification, high-performance buildings, renewable energy systems, and EV infrastructure. Position Details: This position is a part time, salaried position, with a 15-hour work schedule. Please note that this position is also contingent on the availability of external funding and is subject to annual performance reviews and funding renewals . The incumbent may be separated from employment with notice if funding is reduced or discontinued. This position is currently funded with an anticipated end date of December 2028. At this time, the university is unable to sponsor applicants for H-1B visas. The expected yearly salary range for this position is $35,100 which reflects what we reasonably expect to pay for this part-time role. Please note that this is a non-benefits eligible position. Compensation and Benefits Wentworth Institute of Technology is committed to fair, transparent, and legally compliant compensation practices. We believe that clarity about pay structures and ranges supports equity, fosters trust, and ensures a positive workplace for all employees. Please visit here to see the comprehensive benefits package offered to support the best experience for our employees. https://wit.edu/careers/work-wentworth Inclusive Excellence at Wentworth Inclusive Excellence is one of the four pillars of the Strategic Plan. Actively and intentionally cultivating a diverse and culturally competent institution where each member has the opportunity and support to reach their full potential and make contributions to our campus community and beyond is Inclusive Excellence at Wentworth. To find out more about the Wentworth’s commitment to Inclusive Excellence, please visit the website https://wit.edu/about/inclusive-excellence . All applicants have the right to accessibility support and accommodations. To request accessibility support or accommodations, contact the Executive Director of Equity and Compliance, Catlin Wells, at wellsc1@wit.edu . E-Verify for Employment Eligibility Verification ( Form I-9) Wentworth participates in E-Verify. E-Verify is an internet-based system that compares information from your Form I-9 to records available to the U.S. Department of Homeland Security (DHS) and Social Security Administration (SSA) to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States."
    },
    "https://wit.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Boston-MA-US/Laboratory-Instructor-and-Coordinator--Mechanical-Engineering--Thermo-Fluid-and-Aerospace-_JR5245-1": {
      "title": "Laboratory Instructor and Coordinator, Mechanical Engineering (Thermo-Fluid and Aerospace)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Position Summary Reporting primarily to the Dean, with a secondary reporting relationship to the Laboratory Director, the Laboratory Instructor and Coordinator - Mechanical Engineering (Thermo-Fluid and Aerospace), plays a key role in coordinating laboratory operations and delivering high-quality, hands-on instruction in undergraduate engineering laboratories. This position is critical in advancing experiential learning, student success, and continuous program improvement through effective laboratory management, instructional support, and collaboration with faculty. Essential Functions Laboratory Instruction Teach and/or support instruction in undergraduate engineering laboratory courses: Deliver technical demonstrations, guide students in experimental methods, data acquisition, analysis, and technical documentation. Support project-based learning activities, design projects, and prototype development. Grade and assess student laboratory reports, assignments, and projects to support student learning outcomes. Laboratory Coordination & Operations : Coordinate the scheduling, setup, and operation of engineering laboratories. Maintain, troubleshoot, and calibrate laboratory equipment, instruments, and computing resources. Manage laboratory inventory, procurement of supplies, and vendor coordination. Develop and update laboratory manuals, instructional materials, and standard operating procedures. Support senior design projects, student competition teams, and applied research activities. Safety & Compliance : Ensure compliance with institutional laboratory safety policies and applicable state and federal regulations. Maintain safety documentation, inspection records, and risk assessments. Promote a culture of safe laboratory practices and responsible equipment use. Assessment, Accreditation & Continuous Improvement: Access Laboratory Learning Outcomes. Support documentation and data collection for accreditation and program review processes. Contribute to continuous improvement initiatives related to laboratory curriculum and student engagement. Service & Collaboration: Participate in departmental meetings, outreach events, recruitment activities, and open houses. Work collaboratively with faculty, staff, and students to enhance the laboratory learning environment. Provide mentoring and technical guidance to students. Workload / Percent Effort Instruction (lab delivery, instruction of record, grading): 20–40% (covering ~10 credits of lab instruction per year). Lab coordination, preparation, student support, and operational responsibilities: 60–80%. Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree in Engineering or related field. Preferred Qualifications Three years of industry Experience. Experience with laboratory instruction, grading, and student assessment. Position Details At this time, the university is unable to sponsor applicants for H-1B visas. The job grade for this position is Grade 8. The expected salary for this position is between $78,000.00 - $98,000.00 which reflects what we reasonably expect to pay for this role. Compensation and Benefits Wentworth Institute of Technology is committed to fair, transparent, and legally compliant compensation practices. We believe that clarity about pay structures and ranges supports equity, fosters trust, and ensures a positive workplace for all employees. Please visit here to see the comprehensive benefits package offered to support the best experience for our employees. https://wit.edu/careers/work-wentworth Inclusive Excellence at Wentworth Inclusive Excellence is one of the four pillars of the Strategic Plan. Actively and intentionally cultivating a diverse and culturally competent institution where each member has the opportunity and support to reach their full potential and make contributions to our campus community and beyond is Inclusive Excellence at Wentworth. To find out more about the Wentworth’s commitment to Inclusive Excellence, please visit the website https://wit.edu/about/inclusive-excellence . All applicants have the right to accessibility support and accommodations. To request accessibility support or accommodations, contact the Executive Director of Equity and Compliance, Catlin Wells, at wellsc1@wit.edu . E-Verify for Employment Eligibility Verification ( Form I-9) Wentworth participates in E-Verify. E-Verify is an internet-based system that compares information from your Form I-9 to records available to the U.S. Department of Homeland Security (DHS) and Social Security Administration (SSA) to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States."
    },
    "https://wit.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Boston-MA-US/Head-Coach--Men-s-Ice-Hockey_JR5243-1": {
      "title": "Head Coach, Men’s Ice Hockey",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Position Summary Wentworth Institute of Technology invites applications for the position of Head Men's Ice Hockey Coach. This full-time, 12-month administrative position provides leadership for all aspects of the University's NCAA Division III men's ice hockey program, including student-athlete development, competitive success, recruitment, program administration, and strategic planning. Consistent with Wentworth's strategic priorities of Inclusive Excellence, Transformative Student Experience, and High-Value Learning, the Head Coach creates an environment where students are challenged academically, athletically, and personally while representing Wentworth with professionalism, integrity, and a commitment to the University's mission and values. The Head Coach serves as an educator, mentor, and leader who develops a culture of accountability, belonging, teamwork, competitive excellence, and continuous improvement. The successful candidate will provide strategic leadership for all aspects of the program while developing student-athletes, hiring, supervising, mentoring, and evaluating assistant coaches, collaborating with colleagues across the University, responsibly stewarding program resources, and strengthening relationships with alumni, supporters, and external partners in support of the long-term success of Wentworth Men's Ice Hockey. SCOPE OF RESPONSIBILITY Program Leadership & Administration The Head Coach provides strategic leadership and administrative oversight for all aspects of the NCAA Division III men's ice hockey program, establishing competitive goals, setting program expectations, and cultivating a positive, accountable, and student-centered team culture. The Head Coach oversees the day-to-day operations of the program, including: planning and conducting practices; preparing for competition; developing game strategy; scheduling contests; coordinating team travel; overseeing equipment management; and evaluating program performance. The Head Coach manages the program budget, supports fundraising and alumni engagement initiatives, and fulfills all fiscal and administrative responsibilities in a timely and responsible manner. The Head Coach is responsible for recruiting, supervising, and mentoring a part-time assistant coaching staff by providing ongoing mentorship, regular feedback, and opportunities for professional development. Because Wentworth utilizes external athletic facilities for the Men’s Ice Hockey Program, the Head Coach develops and maintains productive relationships with FMC Ice Sports at the Allied Veterans Rink in Everett and other facility partners to ensure effective scheduling and operations. Recruitment & Enrollment Recruitment at Wentworth is viewed as the foundational step of long-term student retention and success. The Head Men’s Ice Hockey Coach provides strategic leadership for recruiting and roster management that reflects the values of Wentworth Institute of Technology and the Wentworth Athletics Department. Working collaboratively with Enrollment Management and Athletics and Student Affairs leadership, the Head Coach develops and executes an annual recruiting strategy that supports institutional and program enrollment goals while identifying student-athletes who will thrive academically, socially, and competitively at Wentworth. The Head Coach is expected to cultivate relationships with prospects and their families, clearly articulating the unique value of a Wentworth education and the University's commitment to student success and professional development. Student-Athlete Development Beyond competition, the Head Coach is committed to the holistic development of student-athletes by promoting academic success, leadership development, personal well-being, and competitive excellence. To achieve this, the Head Coach actively partners with cross-institutional colleagues to support student well-being, academic achievement, leadership development, personal accountability, and overall student success. Encourages student-athletes to engage fully in the academic, leadership, and co-curricular opportunities available through the University. Departmental & Institutional Engagement Alongside primary coaching duties, full-time head coaches are assigned a secondary duty/administrative responsibility which are reviewed and assigned annually based on the candidate’s qualifications, seasonal responsibilities, and department needs.   Additionally, full-time head coaches support Athletics Department operations through game management responsibilities, conference and NCAA championship administration, and departmental signature events.  Serves as an active member of the Division of Student Affairs and the Athletics Department by contributing to divisional and departmental planning, committee work, collaborative initiatives, and a shared commitment to student-athlete success. Builds and maintains collaborative relationships with faculty, staff, and departments across the University to support student success and advance departmental, divisional, and institutional priorities. Represents Wentworth Athletics and the University at institutional, conference, alumni, community, and professional events, serving as a positive ambassador for the athletics department and the University. Compliance & Professional Responsibilities Maintains required certifications, completes mandatory institutional training, and fulfills administrative responsibilities in a timely manner. Ensures compliance with NCAA Division III legislation, Conference of New England policies, University policies, and all applicable federal and state regulations. QUALIFICATIONS Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree required. Minimum of five years of demonstrated success coaching ice hockey, including progressive leadership responsibilities. Demonstrated ability to recruit and retain academically qualified student-athletes. Valid driver’s license.  Demonstrated strong communication skills and experience building inclusive team environments. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree. Collegiate coaching experience, preferably at the NCAA level. Five to seven years of collegiate coaching experience with previous head coaching or significant assistant coaching leadership responsibilities. Position Details At this time, the university is unable to sponsor applicants for H-1B visas. The job grade for this position is Grade 7. The expected salary for this position is between $71,000.00 - $85,000.00 which reflects what we reasonably expect to pay for this role. Required Application Materials: Resume and Cover Letter Compensation and Benefits Wentworth Institute of Technology is committed to fair, transparent, and legally compliant compensation practices. We believe that clarity about pay structures and ranges supports equity, fosters trust, and ensures a positive workplace for all employees. Please visit here to see the comprehensive benefits package offered to support the best experience for our employees. https://wit.edu/careers/work-wentworth Inclusive Excellence at Wentworth Inclusive Excellence is one of the four pillars of the Strategic Plan. Actively and intentionally cultivating a diverse and culturally competent institution where each member has the opportunity and support to reach their full potential and make contributions to our campus community and beyond is Inclusive Excellence at Wentworth. To find out more about the Wentworth’s commitment to Inclusive Excellence, please visit the website https://wit.edu/about/inclusive-excellence . All applicants have the right to accessibility support and accommodations. To request accessibility support or accommodations, contact the Executive Director of Equity and Compliance, Catlin Wells, at wellsc1@wit.edu . E-Verify for Employment Eligibility Verification ( Form I-9) Wentworth participates in E-Verify. E-Verify is an internet-based system that compares information from your Form I-9 to records available to the U.S. Department of Homeland Security (DHS) and Social Security Administration (SSA) to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States."
    },
    "https://wit.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Boston-MA-US/Assistant-Vice-President-for-Development_JR5232": {
      "title": "Assistant Vice President for Development",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-17\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Wentworth Institute of Technology | Boston, MA | Hybrid About Wentworth Institute of Technology Wentworth is a private, STEM and design-focused university in Boston's Fenway neighborhood, founded in 1904, with 45,000+ living alumni. Ninety-one percent of graduates are employed or in graduate school within six months, and every undergraduate completes two paid co-op semesters. Wentworth closed FY25 with more than $40 million in new commitments, well above prior years, including the largest single gift in institutional history. The Opportunity The Vice President for University Advancement, Derek Berger, seeks a senior development leader to lead the gift officer team through The Campaign for Wentworth, a comprehensive campaign organized around four priorities: student access and success, next-generation learning, campus spaces, and unrestricted support through the Wentworth Fund. The campaign is currently in its quiet phase, with a public launch planned for 2029 and completion in 2031, and this is the campaign the next AVP will carry to the finish, contributing to the strategy, prospect readiness, and leadership giving that position it to go public, then leading the team toward the close. The AVP serves as the Vice President's senior partner on fundraising strategy. The team has produced back-to-back record fundraising years; what this role adds is reach. The AVP engages at a level of seniority that generates opportunities the team can develop and close, and converts an untapped industry pipeline built through more than fifty years of co-op relationships in life sciences, technology, construction, and real estate. Key Responsibilities Lead the gift officer team, spanning major gifts, leadership gifts, and industry, foundation, and government partnerships Carry a personal portfolio of major and principal gift prospects Partner with the Vice President and President on the university's most transformational donor relationships Hold the team accountable using pipeline data, portfolio metrics, and performance indicators, with a regular cadence of moves-management reviews Develop gift officers into Wentworth's next generation of advancement leaders through direct coaching Steward gift-acceptance and naming decisions across a 10-year Institutional Master Plan with naming potential at every level of the gift table Qualifications 10+ years of frontline fundraising experience with a demonstrated history of closing major gifts Direct participation in a comprehensive campaign at the $50M level or above Experience managing a development team during a campaign Experience with principal gift strategies at the seven-figure level and above Strong working knowledge of moves management, pipeline development, and CRM systems such as Slate Ability to analyze fundraising data and use metrics to drive program decisions Position Details At this time, the university is unable to sponsor applicants for H-1B visas. The job grade for this position is Grade 12. $165,000 to $185,000, with comprehensive health, dental, and vision coverage, retirement plan participation, generous leave, and the full range of university benefits. Based on Wentworth's Fenway campus, hybrid with roughly three days in the office, with regional travel and some national presence. How to Apply Catalyst is leading this search on behalf of Wentworth Institute of Technology. Submit a resume and letter of interest addressed to the Search Committee, in confidence, to WentworthAVP@catalystcampaign.com. View the position prospectus here: Wentworth AVP Prospectus Compensation and Benefits Wentworth Institute of Technology is committed to fair, transparent, and legally compliant compensation practices. We believe that clarity about pay structures and ranges supports equity, fosters trust, and ensures a positive workplace for all employees. Please visit here to see the comprehensive benefits package offered to support the best experience for our employees. https://wit.edu/careers/work-wentworth Inclusive Excellence at Wentworth Inclusive Excellence is one of the four pillars of the Strategic Plan. Actively and intentionally cultivating a diverse and culturally competent institution where each member has the opportunity and support to reach their full potential and make contributions to our campus community and beyond is Inclusive Excellence at Wentworth. To find out more about the Wentworth’s commitment to Inclusive Excellence, please visit the website https://wit.edu/about/inclusive-excellence . All applicants have the right to accessibility support and accommodations. To request accessibility support or accommodations, contact the Executive Director of Equity and Compliance, Catlin Wells, at wellsc1@wit.edu . E-Verify for Employment Eligibility Verification ( Form I-9) Wentworth participates in E-Verify. E-Verify is an internet-based system that compares information from your Form I-9 to records available to the U.S. Department of Homeland Security (DHS) and Social Security Administration (SSA) to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States."
